card c09
kind: teach
type: story
tier: deeper
scored: 0
title: An idea before the proof
speaker: npc-hal
tag: Ancient Greece
figure: halving
figure_at: 2

body:
    About 2,400 years ago the Greek thinker Democritus asked what would happen if you kept cutting something in half. He imagined a smallest piece that could not be cut, and called it atomos. Seeing atoms took far longer.
